			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				39,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Worker): Add Security, Compatibility, License, and Changelog sections to README\n\nExpand the Worker README with four new documentation sections:\n\n**Security** — document the multi-layer security architecture: Trusted Types enforcement via the `WorkerApplication` policy, auth token encryption, CSP compliance, scope isolation to `/Application` paths, and build-time sealing of environment variables.\n\n**Compatibility** — tabulate integration points with sister elements (Sky, Wind, Cocoon) and the Tauri WebView runtime, clarifying how Worker interacts with each.\n\n**License** and **Changelog** — restore license notice and changelog reference as standalone sections with direct links to the project repository files.\n\nAlso clean up the Mermaid diagram labels by removing em-quad spacing characters between text and emoji markers, and add the `title` attribute to the Star badge `<img>` element for accessibility compliance.",
			"SHA": "a464e68e572025756ed35da6fb27c4373a348bc1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:37:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				39,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Worker): Add badge header to Architecture and polish DeepDive opening\n\nAdd the standard Land logo badge (dark/light picture elements) to the\nArchitecture document header, replacing the plain text heading. Restructure\nthe heading to follow the project convention: bold element name with em-quad\nseparated emoji and \"Architecture\" suffix.\n\nRephrase the DeepDive opening sentence from passive framing (\"This document\nprovides...\") to an active element-first framing (\"**Worker** provides...\"),\naligning with the project's documentation style where each element\ndocument opens by foregrounding its component name.\n\nBoth changes are purely cosmetic documentation improvements that bring\nthese files into visual and editorial consistency with sister-element\ndocumentation across the Land project.",
			"SHA": "387f08beff3888b12c8a94313eaf2c68963e6ffa"
		}
